    <div class="page">

        <div class="main-content">
            


<div class="content-page bg-primary ">
    <div class="heading-section color-overlay content-light " style="background-image: url('/-/media/Website/Images/ContentPageBanner.png');background-size:cover;">
        <div class="breadcrumb"></div>
                    <div class="container">
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="heading-content col-1 gold-bar"></div>
                </div>
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="heading-content col-12">
                        <h1>Regulatory Updates</h1>

                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section row content-dark bg-white">
            <div class="sidenav-container col-3">
                        <div class="sidebar-title title-small-border-blue">
            <div class="title">
                <a href="/en/securities-law-and-policy" class="">
                    <i class="gold-bar"></i>
                    Securities Law &amp; Policy
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    <div class="sidebar-nav-list">
            <ul>
                        <li class="child-title">
                            <a href="/en/securities-law-and-policy/act-and-regulation" class="">
                                <i class="gold-bar"></i>
                                Act &amp; Regulation
                            </a>


                        </li>
                        <li class="child-title">
                            <a href="/en/securities-law-and-policy/regulatory-instruments" class="">
                                <i class="gold-bar"></i>
                                Regulatory Instruments
                            </a>


                        </li>
                        <li class="child-title">
                            <a href="/en/securities-law-and-policy/regulatory-updates" class="active">
                                <i class="gold-bar"></i>
                                Regulatory Updates
                            </a>


                        </li>
                        <li class="child-title">
                            <a href="/en/securities-law-and-policy/authorizations-and-memorandums-of-understanding" class="">
                                <i class="gold-bar"></i>
                                Authorizations &amp; Memorandums of Understanding
                            </a>


                        </li>
                        <li class="child-title">
                            <a href="/en/securities-law-and-policy/blanket-orders-and-designation-orders" class="">
                                <i class="gold-bar"></i>
                                Blanket Orders &amp; Designation Orders
                            </a>


                        </li>
            </ul>
    </div>

            </div>

        <div class="container col-lg-9 col-sm-12 body-container color-overlay">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-12">
                    <div class="general-content">
                                                    <div class="body"><p>What's new in regulation at the ASC? Check back often for the latest updates.</p>
<p>NOTE: Until rules or instruments become effective as evidenced by their publication in The Alberta Gazette (see section 225 of the <em>Securities Act</em> (Alberta)), they are subject to non-substantive changes. Should such changes occur, a revised version of the relevant rule or instrument will be published on this website.</p>
<p>Industry and public consultation is an important part of the regulatory process and provides good input into new or revised legislation. When the ASC or the Canadian Securities Administrators (<strong>CSA</strong>) believes new or revised regulation is required, they will typically publish the proposed new documents for public comment.</p>
<p>This icon <img alt="" src="/-/media/Website/Images/icon-ellipsis-bubble.png?h=24&amp;w=28&amp;hash=ED52BDF67728B5714A1F6D50663E9E9D" style="height: 24px; width: 28px;" /> identifies proposals that are currently available for public comment.</p></div>

                        <div class="accordion-list">
    <h5></h5>
    <div class="rendering">
        <div class="container-restraint">

            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-12 columns-content group">
                    <div class="accordion-container">
                        <div class="accordion-items">


                                        <h4>October 2026</h4>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-1">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice of Amendments to National Instrument 31-103 Registration Requirements, Exemptions and Ongoing Registrant Obligations Prohibition on the Use of Chargebacks in the Distribution of Investment Fund Securities  </div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-1">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">October 08, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Canadian Securities Administrators (the CSA or we) are adopting amendments (the Amendments) to National Instrument 31-103 <em>Registration Requirements, Exemptions and Ongoing Registrant Obligations </em>(NI 31-103) to prohibit the use of chargebacks in the distribution of securities of investment funds that are reporting issuers (the Chargeback Ban). Subject to such approvals, the Amendments will come into force on October 1, 2028 excluding certain transition provisions.</p>
<p><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.asc.ca/-/media/ASC-Documents-part-1/Regulatory-Instruments/2026/10/6304440-CSA-Notice-Amendments-to-NI-31-103.pdf" target="_blank">CSA Notice of Amendments to National Instrument 31-103 <em>Registration Requirements, Exemptions and Ongoing Registrant Obligations</em> Prohibition on the Use of Chargebacks in the Distribution of Investment Fund Securities</a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-2">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice regarding Coordinated Blanket Order 23-930 Re Temporary Exemption from Trading Fee Cap Requirements for Inter-listed Securities under National Instrument 23-101 Trading Rules</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-2">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">October 01, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>Today, the Alberta Securities Commission and certain other members of the Canadian Securities Administrators (<strong>CSA</strong>) are publishing a temporary exemption from certain requirements under amendments to National Instrument 23-101 <em>Trading Rules</em> (<strong>NI 23-101</strong>) that will come into force in their jurisdictions on November 2, 2026.</p>
<p>The CSA has coordinated the relief through substantively harmonized local blanket orders in the form of Coordinated Blanket Order 23-930 Re <em>Temporary Exemption from Trading Fee Cap Requirements</em> for Inter-listed Securities under National Instrument 23-101 <em>Trading Rules </em>(collectively, the <strong>Blanket Order</strong>). The Blanket Order is being issued in Alberta, Nova Scotia, Ontario and Prince Edward Island (the <strong>Participating Jurisdictions</strong>).</p>
<p>The Blanket Order will exempt marketplaces from certain new trading fee cap requirements; namely, that a marketplace not charge a fee that is greater than CAD 0.0017 for securities listed on both a Canadian recognized exchange and a U.S. registered national securities exchange (<strong>U.S. Inter-listed Securities</strong>) with an execution price that is greater than or equal to CAD 1.00. It will allow marketplaces to continue to charge a fee that is no greater than CAD 0.0030 per U.S. Inter-listed Security, which, as described below, corresponds with the USD 0.0030 maximum fee for U.S. exchanges that is expected to remain in effect until at least November 1, 2027.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/6DCAE7BD078F4336B9570768F25EA2CA.ashx" target="_blank">CSA Notice regarding Coordinated Blanket Order 23-930 <em>Re Temporary Exemption from Trading Fee Cap Requirements for Inter-listed Securities under National Instrument 23-101 Trading Rules</em><br />
&nbsp;</a></p>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-3">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice and Request for Comment Proposed National Instrument 26-101 Information Technology System Integrity (and related Companion Policy and consequential amendments)</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="/-/media/Website/Images/icon-ellipsis-bubble.png" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-3">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">October 01, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Alberta Securities Commission has published CSA Notice and Request for Comment Proposed National Instrument 26-101 <em>Information Technology System Integrity</em> and Proposed Companion Policy 26-101 <em>Information Technology System Integrity</em>. This Notice publishes for comment the proposed new Instrument and Companion Policy which would establish a single framework for the information technology systems (IT) related to the integrity of market infrastructure entities&rsquo; IT systems.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/66B99C5A2560449D81FC130B0BD7997C.ashx" target="_blank">CSA Notice and Request for Comment Proposed National Instrument 26-101 <em>Information Technology System Integrity</em> (and related Companion Policy and consequential amendments)</a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                        <h4>September 2026</h4>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-4">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice and Request for Comment Proposed Amendments to National Instrument 81-102 Investment Funds Exemptions from Certain Repurchase Transactions Requirements for Investment Funds</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="/-/media/Website/Images/icon-ellipsis-bubble.png" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-4">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">September 17, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Canadian Securities Administrators today published for comment proposed amendments that would provide harmonized exemptions from certain repurchase transactions requirements for reporting issuer investment funds. The proposed amendments are intended to facilitate access to the Bank of Canada's Contingent Term Repo Facility, as well as any future repurchase facilities provided by the Bank of Canada. The proposed amendments would codify the temporary exemptive relief provided by <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.asc.ca/securities-law-and-policy/regulatory-instruments/81-930" target="_blank">Coordinated Blanket Order 81-930 <em>Exemptions from Certain Repurchase Transactions Requirements for Investment Funds</em></a>. </p>
<p>The comment period is open until November 16, 2026.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/C0376A468C4E4A5291AE807D4B786CB0.ashx">CSA Notice and Request for Comment Proposed Amendments to National Instrument 81-102 Investment Funds Exemptions from Certain Repurchase Transactions Requirements for Investment Funds</a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                        <h4>August 2026</h4>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-5">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA/CIRO Staff Notice 91-307 Guidance related to Event Contracts: Compliance with Regulatory Requirements</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-5">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">August 27, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>Staff of the CSA and CIRO are publishing a joint CSA/CIRO Staff Notice 91-307 <em>Guidance related to Event Contracts: Compliance with Regulatory Requirements</em> to provide clarity about how securities regulation applies to products commonly known as &ldquo;event contracts, prediction contracts, or prediction market contracts&rdquo;.<br />
<br />
Specifically, staff state that Event Contracts based on sports and entertainment events or outcomes should not be regulated within securities and derivatives legislation.&nbsp; Further guidance regarding other types of Event Contracts will be forthcoming.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/512055080E3140D1B8FA588DFEFDC3CA.ashx">CSA/CIRO Staff Notice 91-307 <em>Guidance related to Event Contracts: Compliance with Regulatory Requirements</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-6">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">ASC NOTICE 31-701 (Revised) Account Opening Assistance</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-6">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">August 20, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Alberta Securities Commission (&ldquo;ASC&rdquo;) has published ASC Notice 31-701 (Revised) <em>Account Opening Assistance</em>. This Notice includes updates to the Sample Know Your Client form included in the initial (2017) publication. It also introduces a Sample Trusted Contact Person form to assist exempt market dealers and their dealing representatives in meeting the requirements set out in section 13.2.01 <em>Know your client &ndash; trusted contact person</em> of National Instrument 31-103.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/81BD3BD24C8545C68F84A6597F0CE5A9.ashx">ASC NOTICE 31-701 (Revised) <em>Account Opening Assistance</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-7">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Multilateral Notice of Changes to Companion Policy 96-101 Derivatives: Trade Reporting and Policy Statement to Regulation 91-507 Respecting Trade Repositories and Derivatives Data Reporting</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-7">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">August 11, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>Policy Statement to Regulation 91-507 and Companion Policy 96-101 are being changed to provide market participants with an updated version of the CSA derivatives data technical manual (the Manual).&nbsp; The changes to the Manual include updated technical specifications regarding the definition, format and allowable values for each data element that is required to be reported under <em>Regulation 91-507 respecting Trade Repositories and Derivatives Data Reporting</em>, in Qu&eacute;bec, and Multilateral Instrument 96-101 <em>Derivatives: Trade Reporting</em> in the other Participating Jurisdictions. These changes are intended to improve the standardization and harmonisation of data elements.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/30D095FA910A4B2CA33ADD23D4A60557.ashx">CSA Multilateral Notice of Changes to Companion Policy 96-101<em> Derivatives: Trade Reporting</em> and Policy Statement to Regulation 91-507 Respecting <em>Trade Repositories and Derivatives Data Reporting</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                        <h4>July 2026</h4>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-8">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice and Request for Comment Proposed Amendments to National Instrument 45-106 Prospectus Exemptions relating to the Listed Issuer Financing Exemption</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="/-/media/Website/Images/icon-ellipsis-bubble.png" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-8">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">July 23, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Canadian Securities Administrators are publishing for a 90 day comment period, proposed amendments to the listed issuer financing exemption found in National Instrument 45-106 <em>Prospectus Exemptions</em> and Companion Policy 45-106CP <em>Prospectus Exemptions</em>, which propose to increase the amount that can be raised under the exemption and streamline certain other conditions and disclosure requirements of the exemption.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/4F844DB88D2C429C809517A7041FCE22.ashx" target="_blank">CSA Notice and Request for Comment Proposed Amendments to National Instrument 45-106 <em>Prospectus Exemptions</em> relating to the Listed Issuer Financing Exemption</a></p>
<p><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.asc.ca/securities-law-and-policy/regulatory-instruments/45-106" target="_blank">National Instrument 45-106 <em>Prospectus Exemptions</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-9">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Consultation Paper 51-406 Modernizing the Regulation of Public Companies</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="/-/media/Website/Images/icon-ellipsis-bubble.png" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-9">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">July 16, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p><span>The Canadian Securities Administrators are publishing, for a 120 day comment period, a consultation paper seeking feedback on how to support a regulatory framework for reporting issuers that facilitates access to capital, supports the competitiveness of Canadian capital markets and appropriately balances investor protection.</span></p>
<p><a href="-/media/4EED0598A40741D3B1A558C9F9F8623F.ashx" target="_blank">CSA Consultation Paper 51-406 <em>Modernizing the Regulation of Public Companies</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-10">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Staff Notice 33-322 Review of Registered Firms’ Cybersecurity Practices and Additional Guidance</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-10">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">July 15, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Canadian Securities Administrators (<strong>CSA</strong>) published a notice today that sets out the findings of CSA staff during a recent targeted compliance sweep focused on cyber security. Included in the notice is a description of some of the industry best practices that were observed during the sweep. CSA staff publish this notice to provide market participants with information that may be helpful in identifying risks and improving cyber security policies and procedures</p>
<p><a href="-/media/E410D18820394BF3A4EC1860E2E757F6.ashx" target="_blank">CSA Staff Notice 33-322 <em>Review of Registered Firms&rsquo; Cybersecurity Practices and Additional Guidance</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                        <h4>June 2026</h4>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-11">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Staff Notice 21-335 Information Processor for Exchange-Traded Securities other than Options</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-11">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">June 25, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Canadian Securities Administrators have determined that TMX Information Processor (TMX IP) will continue to act as an information processor (IP) for exchange-traded securities other than options under National Instrument 21-101 <em>Marketplace Operation </em>(NI 21-101) until June 30, 2029. In Ontario, Saskatchewan, Alberta, and British Columbia, TMX IP will be designated as an IP and subject to terms and conditions contained in a designation order. In Qu&eacute;bec, TMX IP will be recognized as an IP and subject to terms and conditions outlined in a recognition order. In all other jurisdictions, TMX IP will operate pursuant to a number of undertakings (which are similar to the terms and conditions set out in the Ontario, Saskatchewan, Alberta, British Columbia, and Qu&eacute;bec orders).</p>
<p><a href="-/media/17436C76DC0749E2A9025E25147DB638.ashx" target="_blank">CSA Staff Notice 21-335 <em>Information Processor for Exchange-Traded Securities other than Options</em></a><br />
&nbsp;</p>
<div>&nbsp;</div></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-12">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice of Amendments and Changes to Implement an Access Model for Certain Continuous Disclosure Documents of Non-Investment Fund Reporting Issuers</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-12">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">June 25, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Canadian Securities Administrators (CSA) today published in final form amendments and changes to implement an access model for certain continuous disclosure documents of reporting issuers, other than investment funds (the <strong>Access Model</strong>). The Access Model aims to modernize the way annual financial statements, interim financial reports and related management&rsquo;s discussion &amp; analysis (collectively, <strong>CD documents</strong>) are made available to investors by providing alternative procedures whereby electronic access may be provided to CD documents instead of following the delivery requirements currently found in securities legislation. Among the measures implemented to support this change, the CSA has developed SEDAR+ notification functionality that a person or company can use to subscribe to receive an email notification when the CD documents that they subscribed for have been filed by the issuer on SEDAR+.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/5C682BCE7AEA48B786DBC6A25CD85263.ashx">CSA Notice of Amendments and Changes to Implement an Access Model for Certain Continuous Disclosure Documents of Non-Investment Fund Reporting Issuers</a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-13">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice Regarding Coordinated Blanket Order 31-935 Exemption from the Client Reporting Requirements for Certain Institutional Clients and Overflow Accounts of Registered Advisers</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-13">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">June 25, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Canadian Securities Administrators published Coordinated Blanket Order 31-935 <em>Exemption from the client reporting requirements for certain institutional clients and overflow accounts of registered advisers</em> (the <strong>Blanket Order</strong>) in order to grant registered advisers exemptive relief from client reporting requirements in respect of certain institutional clients and overflow accounts.&nbsp; The Blanket Order comes into effect on June 25, 2026, and expires on the date on which regulatory or legislative amendments come into force that address substantially the same subject matter as the Blanket Order.</p>
<p><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.asc.ca/securities-law-and-policy/regulatory-instruments/31-935" target="_blank">CSA Notice Regarding Coordinated Blanket Order 31-935 <em>Exemption from the Client Reporting Requirements for Certain Institutional Clients and Overflow Accounts of Registered Advisers</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-14">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice of Amendments to National Instrument 31-103 Registration Requirements, Exemptions and Ongoing Registrant Obligations, National Instrument 81-101 Mutual Fund Prospectus Disclosure, National Instrument 81-102 Investment Funds and National Instrument 81-105 Mutual Fund Sales Practices and changes to related Companion Policies regarding the Principal Distributor Model</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-14">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">June 11, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Alberta Securities Commission (&ldquo;Commission&rdquo;) has adopted amendments to National Instrument 81-105 <em>Mutual Fund Sales Practices</em> to clarify that a dealer may act as a principal distributor only for mutual funds in the same mutual fund family. The amendments do not affect the ability of a principal distributor to also distribute mutual fund securities of multiple mutual fund families as a participating dealer. The Commission has also adopted amendments to National Instrument 31-103 <em>Registration Requirements, Exemptions and Ongoing Registrant Obligations</em>, and National Instrument 81-101 <em>Mutual Fund Prospectus Disclosure</em>, to enhance transparency by requiring disclosure of principal distributor arrangements and related compensation in the prospectus, fund facts document and the annual report on charges and other compensation. The Commission has also adopted amendments to National Instrument 81-102 <em>Investment Funds</em> to expressly prohibit a fund manager from charging redemption fees. Related companion policy changes have also been made.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/6A95FDEA58FF48559C6B028F6DA6D6EC.ashx">CSA Notice of Amendments to National Instrument 31-103 <em>Registration Requirements, Exemptions and Ongoing Registrant Obligations</em>, National Instrument 81-101<em> Mutual Fund Prospectus Disclosure</em>, National Instrument 81-102 <em>Investment Funds</em> and National Instrument 81-105 Mutual Fund Sales Practices and changes to related Companion Policies regarding the Principal Distributor Model</a></p>
<br /></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                        <h4>May 2026</h4>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-15">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice and Request for Comment Proposed Amendments and Changes to the Issuer Bid, Take-Over Bid and Beneficial Ownership Reporting Regimes</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="/-/media/Website/Images/icon-ellipsis-bubble.png" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-15">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">May 14, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Canadian Securities Administrators (<strong>CSA</strong>) published today for a 90 day comment period proposed amendments and changes to the Canadian issuer bid, take-over bid, and beneficial ownership reporting regimes. The proposed amendments and changes are intended to provide issuers with greater flexibility to repurchase their own securities, enhance transparency of ownership of derivative interests in specified circumstances, and reduce regulatory burden and enhance the integrity of the issuer bid, take-over bid, and early warning reporting regimes through clarifying amendments and supplemental policy guidance.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/59D37EBAC5DE43CEA0D6332D09EE535E.ashx" target="_blank">CSA Notice and Request for Comment <em>Proposed Amendments and Changes to the Issuer Bid, Take-Over Bid and Beneficial Ownership Reporting Regimes</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                        <h4>April 2026</h4>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-16">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice regarding Coordinated Blanket Order 33-930 Exemptions from Requirements to Submit Certain Personal Information Under National Instrument 33-109 Registration Information</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-16">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">April 30, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>Effective May 1, 2026, the Canadian Securities Administrators (CSA) will be adopting Coordinated Blanket Order 33-930 <em>Exemptions from Requirements to Submit Certain Personal Information</em>, which provides temporary exemptions under National Instrument 33-109 <em>Registration Information</em>. The coordinated blanket order removes certain requirements to provide personal information that the CSA has determined is not required for identification in this context.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/E0326F1C5A8C41E8B44E4B0BDFBC5656.ashx" target="_blank">CSA Notice regarding Coordinated Blanket Order 33-930 <em>Exemptions from Requirements to Submit Certain Personal Information Under National Instrument 33-109 Registration Information</em></a></p>
<p><a href="-/media/48F2C65DEA5041C291F17FECA1081BC7.ashx" target="_blank">Coordinated Blanket Order 33-930 <em>Exemptions from Requirements to Submit Certain Personal Information Under National Instrument 33-109 Registration Information</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-17">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice of Amendments to National Instrument 23-101 Trading Rules and Changes to Companion Policy</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-17">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">April 23, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>Today, the Canadian Securities Administrators are adopting amendments to National Instrument 23-101 <em>Trading Rules</em> (NI 23-101 or the Instrument) and changes to Companion Policy 23-101 <em>Trading Rules</em> (the CP).</p>
<p><a href="-/media/49C2AD8CD5E344CEB056B2103E6F9CC8.ashx">CSA Notice of Amendments to National Instrument 23-101 <em>Trading Rules</em> and Changes to Companion Policy</a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-18">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Staff Notice 25-315 2025 Annual Activities Report on the Oversight of the Canadian Investment Regulatory Organization and the Canadian Investor Protection Fund</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-18">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">April 02, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>CSA Position Paper 25-404 <em>A New Self-Regulatory Organization Framework</em> established the CSA&rsquo;s intention to publish an annual activities report on the CSA&rsquo;s oversight of the Self Regulatory Organization (SRO) and IPF (Investor Protection Fund), for the purpose of improving transparency with the public regarding ongoing oversight activities.</p>
<p>This report summarizes key oversight activities of CSA staff and their assessment of CIRO and CIPF compliance with securities legislation requirements, including the terms and conditions of recognition or approval.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/A620B85BC17E46B99018A27255F36923.ashx" target="_blank">CSA Staff Notice 25-315 2025<em> Annual Activities Report on the Oversight of the Canadian Investment Regulatory Organization and the Canadian Investor Protection Fund</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                        <h4>March 2026</h4>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-19">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">ASC Notice 31-702 ASC Registration Fees and CIRO Approved Person Fees for Alberta-Resident Individual Registrants for 2026</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-19">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">March 30, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Alberta Securities Commission (<strong>ASC</strong>) has issued Staff Notice 31-702 <em>ASC</em> <em>Registration Fees and CIRO Approved Person Fees for Alberta Resident Individual Registrants</em>, outlining a one-year, coordinated approach with the Canadian Investment Regulatory Organization (<strong>CIRO</strong>) to provide a net neutral impact on registration fees for Alberta-resident Approved Persons (AP) for 2026. Following the delegation of certain registration functions to CIRO in 2025, CIRO&rsquo;s annual AP fee is increasing to $300 (from $250) effective April 1, 2026. ASC registration fees were collected as of December 31, 1025. To avoid Alberta-resident APs bearing an additional cost in this transition year, the ASC and CIRO have agreed to a process whereby CIRO will reduce its AP fee by $50 for applicable Alberta-resident APs, and the ASC will pay CIRO $50 per Alberta-resident AP. This coordinated approach enables CIRO to recover costs tied to its expanded responsibilities while maintaining fee neutrality for Alberta-resident individual registrants in 2026. Full details are set out in ASC Staff Notice 31-702.</p>
<p><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.asc.ca/-/media/ASC-Documents-part-1/Regulatory-Instruments/2026/03/6272472-ASC-Notice-31-702-Registration-Fees-and-CIRO-Approved-Person-Fees.pdf" target="_blank">ASC Notice 31-702 <em>ASC Registration Fees and CIRO Approved Person Fees for Alberta-Resident Individual Registrants for 2026</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-20">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice of Coordinated Blanket Order 51-933 Exemptions to Permit Semi-Annual Reporting for Certain Venture Issuers</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-20">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">March 19, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Canadian Securities Administrators have today announced <span>a multi-year pilot to allow eligible issuers to voluntarily adopt semi-annual financial reporting (the <strong>SAR Pilot</strong>) and published Coordinated Blanket Order 51-933 <em>Exemptions to Permit Semi-Annual Reporting for Certain Venture Issuers</em>. The SAR Pilot provides an exemption for certain issuers listed on the TSX Venture Exchange Inc. or the CNSX Markets Inc. from the requirement to file first quarter and third quarter financial reports under National Instrument 51-102 <em>Continuous Disclosure Obligations</em>.</span></p>
<p><span><a href="-/media/B1D66F8A4F3446F0B5BF857BA2C36F7B.ashx" target="_blank">CSA Notice of Coordinated Blanket Order 51-933 <em>Exemptions to Permit Semi-Annual Reporting for Certain Venture Issuers</em></a></span></p>
<p><span><a href="-/media/A3C11ED8C6AE4CB29AA92277EC4314D4.ashx" target="_blank">Coordinated Blanket Order 51-933 <em>Exemptions to Permit Semi-Annual Reporting for Certain Venture Issuers</em></a></span></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                        <h4>January 2026</h4>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-21">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice of Amendments to NI 81-101, NI 81-102, NI 81-106, NI 81-107 and Changes to the Commentary in NI 81-107 re: Modernization of the Continuous Disclosure Regime for Investment Funds.</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-21">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">January 22, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Alberta Securities Commission adopted amendments to National Instrument 81-101 <em>Mutual Fund Prospectus Disclosure</em>, National Instrument 81-102<em> Investment Funds</em>, National Instrument 81-106 <em>Investment Fund Continuous Disclosure</em>, National Instrument 81-107 <em>Independent Review Committee for Investment Funds</em> and related consequential amendments and changes (collectively, the <strong>Final Amendments</strong>). The Final Amendments are designed to reduce the regulatory burden on investment fund managers while maintaining the quality and timeliness of disclosure for investors.</p>
<p><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.asc.ca/-/media/ASC-Documents-part-1/Regulatory-Instruments/2026/01/6265698v1-CSA-Notice-of-Amendments-8-series-re-Modernization-of-the-Continuous-Disclosure-Regime-for.pdf" target="_blank">CSA Notice of Amendments to NI 81-101, NI 81-102, NI 81-106, NI 81-107 and Changes to the Commentary in NI 81-107 re: <em>Modernization of the Continuous Disclosure Regime for Investment Funds</em>.</a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-22">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Staff Notice 96-307 Frequently Asked Questions about Derivatives Trade Reporting (Revised)</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-22">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">January 21, 2026</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>Staff of the CSA is publishing a revised CSA Staff Notice 96-307 <em>Frequently Asked Questions about Derivatives Trade Reporting</em> to provide additional clarity about how certain requirements under the CSA trade reporting rules, including MI 96-101 <em>Derivatives: Trade Reporting</em>, as amended on July 25, 2025, should be implemented.&nbsp;</p>
<p><a href="-/media/971B633EAAB248749930CBFA41879183.ashx">CSA Staff Notice 96-307 <em>Frequently Asked Questions about Derivatives Trade Reporting</em> (Revised)</a></p>
<br /></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                        <h4>December 2025</h4>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-23">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">Joint Canadian Securities Administrators and Canadian Investment Regulatory Organization Staff Notice 31-369 Guidance on the Application of Securities Legislation to Finfluencer Activity</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-23">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">December 11, 2025</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>Today, staff of the Canadian Securities Administrators and the Canadian Investment Regulatory Organization are publishing Staff Notice 31-369 Guidance on the Application of Securities Legislation to Finfluencer Activity. The Notice provides guidance on how securities laws apply to the activities of social media financial influencers (finfluencers) and to registrants and issuers who work with them.</p>
<p><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.asc.ca/-/media/ASC-Documents-part-1/Regulatory-Instruments/2025/12/6258759-CSA-CIRO-Notice-31-369-Finfluencer.pdf" target="_blank">Joint Canadian Securities Administrators and Canadian Investment Regulatory Organization Staff Notice 31-369 <em>Guidance on the Application of Securities Legislation to Finfluencer Activity</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-24">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">Data Fees Methodology Committee Report and Next Steps</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-24">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">December 05, 2025</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Canadian Securities Administrators (CSA) is pleased to share the publication of the <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.securities-administrators.ca/investor-tools/publications/#dfm" target="_blank">Data Fees Methodology (DFM) Committee Report (the <strong>DFM Report</strong>)</a>, developed as part of Stage I of the CSA&rsquo;s broader initiative to enhance access to real-time market data (RTMD).</p>
<p>This initiative began with the release of <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.asc.ca/-/media/ASC-Documents-part-1/Regulatory-Instruments/2022/11/6049811--21-403-Market-Data-Consultation-Paper.pdf" target="_blank">CSA Consultation Paper 21-403 &ndash; <em>Access to Real-Time Market Data</em></a> in November 2022, followed by <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.asc.ca/-/media/ASC-Documents-part-1/Regulatory-Instruments/2024/04/6151305-CSA-Notice-21-334-Next-Steps-Access-Real-Time-Market-Data.pdf" target="_blank">CSA Staff Notice 21-334 &ndash; <em>Next Steps to Facilitate Access to Real-Time Market Data</em></a> in April 2024 (<strong>April 2024 Staff Notice</strong>). These publications outlined the CSA&rsquo;s commitment to addressing stakeholder concerns and improving transparency, fairness, and accessibility in the RTMD ecosystem.
To advance this work, the CSA retained APIA Scholar, represented by Andreas Park and Katya Malinova, and established a DFM industry committee (the DFM Committee), made up of industry participants including individuals from marketplaces, dealers and industry groups. The DFM Committee was tasked with reviewing the current DFM and developing recommendations for improvement, guided by a formal mandate in the April 2024 Staff Notice.</p>
<p>The CSA received the DFM Report in late July 2025 and has conducted a thorough review of the recommendations. CSA Staff are now preparing to assess the impact and feasibility of the recommendations, including&mdash;the calculated DFM fee ranges and how these fee ranges may influence the fees charged by marketplaces for access to and use of RTMD feeds.</p>
<p>The CSA would like to thank all stakeholders who contributed to this important initiative and look forward to continued collaboration as we work towards a more transparent RTMD framework, including an improved DFM.</p>
<p><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.asc.ca/-/media/ASC-Documents-part-1/Regulatory-Instruments/2025/12/6261057-Access-to-Real-Time-Mkt-Data-_-Data-Fees-Methodology-21-334.pdf" target="_blank">Data Fees Methodology Report</a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                        <h4>November 2025</h4>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-25">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Multilateral Staff Notice 31-367 Notice and Consultation Regarding CSA Coordinated Blanket Order 31-930 Exemption to Allow Exempt Market Dealer Participation in Selling Groups in Offerings of Securities Under a Prospectus</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="/-/media/Website/Images/icon-ellipsis-bubble.png" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-25">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">November 27, 2025</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The securities regulators in Alberta, British Columbia, New Brunswick, Nova Scotia, Ontario, Qu&eacute;bec, and Saskatchewan published CSA Multilateral Staff Notice 31-367 regarding CSA Coordinated Blanket Order 31-930 <em>Exemption to Allow Exempt Market Dealer Participation in Selling Groups in Offerings of Securities under a Prospectus</em> (<strong>CSA BO 31-930</strong>) (the <strong>Notice)</strong>. CSA BO 31-930, published on June 20, 2024, provides a temporary exemption from the restriction in National Instrument 31-103 Registration Requirements, Exemptions and Ongoing Registrant Obligations to allow exempt market dealers to participate in prospectus offerings as members of selling groups, subject to certain limitations.&nbsp; The Notice informs stakeholders that CSA BO 31-930, which expires on December 20, 2025, will not be extended. The Notice also seeks feedback on the exemption provided in the local blanket orders to assist in future policy-making, including to consider whether a revised exemption should be published in the future. </p>
<p>The deadline for comments is January 26, 2026.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/8FA333AB8A34464FAA401C6763CBAA80.ashx" target="_blank">CSA Multilateral Staff Notice 31-367 Notice and Consultation Regarding CSA Coordinated Blanket Order 31-930 <em>Exemption to Allow Exempt Market Dealer Participation in Selling Groups in Offerings of Securities Under a Prospectus</em></a><em><br />
</em></p>
<br /></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-26">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice and Request for Comment Proposed Amendments to National Instrument 52-112 Non-GAAP and Other Financial Measures Disclosure</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="/-/media/Website/Images/icon-ellipsis-bubble.png" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-26">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">November 13, 2025</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Canadian Securities Administrators are proposing amendments to ensure that measures that have historically been subject to the requirements of NI 52-112 remain subject to its requirements following the adoption of a new IFRS Accounting Standard. IFRS 18 <em>Presentation and Disclosure in Financial Statements</em>, which will be effective for annual reporting periods beginning on or after January 1, 2027, requires disclosure of management-defined performance measures in the notes to the financial statements. Without the proposed amendments, these measures, that have historically been considered non-GAAP financial measures, would not be subject to the disclosure requirements in NI 52-112 when disclosed outside of the financial statements.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/5D0F1C19A95E4043BCD972D485CACDDC.ashx" target="_blank">CSA Notice and Request for Comment Proposed Amendments to National Instrument 52-112 <em>Non-GAAP and Other Financial Measures Disclosure</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-27">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Staff Notice 11-312 (Revised) National Numbering System</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-27">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">November 13, 2025</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>Today, staff of the Canadian Securities Administrators (CSA) are publishing revisions to Staff Notice 11-312 (Revised) <em>National Numbering System</em> (Notice).&nbsp; The CSA follows a system in which securities regulatory instruments are assigned numbers that indicate the type and subject matter of the instrument.&nbsp; &nbsp;The primary revisions to the Notice add new subcategory 6 to subject matter category 2 (26-xxx &ndash; Other Requirements) and revises the title of third digit 4 (xx-4xx &ndash; CSA Consultation Paper).</p>
<p><a href="-/media/A1394AFF774D459495ABA01F48F346B9.ashx">CSA Staff Notice 11-312 (Revised) <em>National Numbering System</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                        <h4>September 2025</h4>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-28">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10"> ASC Notice Amendments to ASC Rules (General), and Changes to ASC Policy 12-601 Applications Submitted to the Alberta Securities Commission, and ASC Policy 15-601 Whistleblower Program</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-28">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">September 30, 2025</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Alberta Securities Commission published today amendments to the <em>Alberta Securities Rules</em> (General) (<strong>ASC Rules General</strong>). The amendments specify that reporting issuers and specified other market participants, including those engaged in investor relations activities maintain books and records for a period of 7 years.&nbsp; Currently, these parties are required to maintain books and records in relation to their business transactions, financial affairs, and transactions execution on behalf of others, however there is no prescribed time period for how long these books and records must be kept.&nbsp; The amendments will provide these parties with clarity in regards to how long these books and records must be maintained under Alberta securities laws.<br />
<a href="-/media/C1AF4834E20D473EB1CABB2701D10DE0.ashx"></a></p>
<p><a href="-/media/C1AF4834E20D473EB1CABB2701D10DE0.ashx">ASC Notice Amendments to <em>ASC Rules</em> (General), and Changes to ASC Policy 12-601 <em>Applications Submitted to the Alberta Securities Commission</em>, and ASC Policy 15-601 <em>Whistleblower Program</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-29">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Multilateral Notice and Request for Comment – Proposed Multilateral Instrument 45-111 Self-Certified Investor Prospectus Exemption and related Companion Policy</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="/-/media/Website/Images/icon-ellipsis-bubble.png" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-29">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">September 25, 2025</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The securities regulatory authorities in Alberta, Manitoba, New Brunswick, Newfoundland and Labrador, Northwest Territories, Nova Scotia, Nunavut, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, Saskatchewan, and Yukon are publishing for a 90-day comment period proposed Multilateral Instrument 45-111 <em>Self-Certified Investor Prospectus Exemption</em>. The proposed instrument will provide a prospectus exemption to Canadian issuers to allow investment by investors with relevant education and/or investment experience. The proposed instrument aims to promote capital formation by enabling a broader spectrum of investors to participate in financing opportunities while ensuring appropriate investor protection. To mitigate the risk of loss for an investor under the proposed instrument who meets the criteria for a self-certified investor, there is a proposed maximum annual investment limit of $50,000 per investor.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/1BEE4E0981BC4AE1BC7821C4DEB1A204.ashx">CSA Multilateral Notice and Request for Comment &ndash; Proposed Multilateral Instrument 45-111 <em>Self-Certified Investor Prospectus Exemption and related Companion Policy</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-30">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice of Amendments to National Instrument 94-101 Mandatory Central Counterparty Clearing of Derivatives</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-30">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">September 25, 2025</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Alberta Securities Commission, together with all the other members of the Canadian Securities Administrators, are publishing final amendments to National Instrument 94-101 <em>Mandatory Central Counterparty Clearing of Derivatives</em> (<strong>National Instrument 94-101</strong>). The amendments to National Instrument 94-101 (the <strong>Amendments</strong>) update the list of mandatory clearable derivatives to reflect global interest rate benchmark reform involving the transition to new overnight risk-free interest rate benchmarks. Specifically, the Amendments reflect the cessation of certain inter-bank offered rates (<strong>IBORs</strong>) and the Canadian dollar offered rate (<strong>CDOR</strong>). The Amendments also add to the list of mandatory clearable derivatives certain types of swaps shown to be increasing in liquidity, including credit default swaps (<strong>CDS</strong>) referencing certain indexes.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/0E747D6340CE4969A99B8DF02AC62487.ashx">CSA Notice of Amendments to National Instrument 94-101 <em>Mandatory Central Counterparty Clearing of Derivatives</em></a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                        <h4>August 2025</h4>
                                    <div class="section">
                                        <a class="menu-item section-header fs-regular row no-gutters" data-target=".tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-31">
                                            <div class="col-lg-10 col-10">CSA Notice of Amendments to National Instrument 44-102 Shelf Distributions Relating to Well-known Seasoned Issuers</div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1 text-right"><span class="comment"><img src="" /></span></div>
                                            <div class="col-lg-1 col-1"><span class="arrow"></span></div>

                                        </a>
                                        <div class="dropdown tab-shortguid-49A603E7159245D6A123ED7042BAEA94-31">
                                            <div class="height-spacer container">

                                                    <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                        <div class="col-12 columns-content date">August 28, 2025</div>
                                                    </div>
                                                <div class="row no-gutters">
                                                    <div class="col-12 columns-content"><p>The Canadian Securities Administrators has today published amendments to National Instrument 44-102 <em>Shelf Distributions</em> that introduce an expedited shelf prospectus regime for well-known seasoned issuers in Canada.</p>
<p><a href="-/media/7CC627A1956B4467805E155759A381CC.ashx">CSA Notice of Amendments to National Instrument 44-102 <em>Shelf Distributions</em> Relating to Well-known Seasoned Issuers</a></p></div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</div>

    <script src="/js/accordian-list.js?v=2.0"></script>



                        


                        


                        


                        

                        

